**Key verifications for the non-obvious L positions:**
- **$N=16$:** divisors $>1$ and $<16$ are $\{2,4,8\}$, all **W**; $16-1=15$ is **W**. Every move leads to **W**, so $16$ is **L**.
- **$N=34$:** divisors $\{2,17\}$; $2$ is **W**, $17$ is **W** (since $17\to16$ which is **L**); $34-1=33$ is **W** (since $33\to3$ or $11$, both **L**). Every move leads to **W**, so $34$ is **L**.

All other composites in range have at least one divisor (or the $N-1$ move) landing on an **L** position, hence are **W**. All primes $p\ge 3$ except $p=17$ satisfy $p-1\in W$ (so $p$ is **L**); $p=17$ has $17-1=16\in L$, so $17$ is **W**; $p=2$ has $2-1=1\in L$, so $2$ is **W**.

